@NVIDIA/mcore-oncall I have completed an author-delegated, AI-assisted line-by-line review and pushed a follow-up correcting the BERT exception-note expectation: the TE projection class is constructed directly, so its name is not a factory note. Current head: `b845d074a8efd783312407217726b2f5ac643aa0`.

Fresh native Windows constructor regressions: baseline 4 failures, patched 4 passes; Ruff lint and syntax checks pass. The PR description records the precise test scope and the remaining GPU/TE limitations.

Could a maintainer vet this head and authorize NVIDIA CI? copy-pr-bot is still waiting for external-contributor validation. I am keeping the PR in draft until CI passes, as requested by the contribution template.

